---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const issues = 'https://github.com/cinic0101/grepsignal/issues/new';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial policy & corrections — GrepSignal" description="What GrepSignal covers, how humans and models contribute, how evidence is reviewed, and how judgments are corrected.">
  <main class="wrap editorial">
    <header class="editorial-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">&gt; show --editorial-contract</div>
      <h1>Evidence. Memory.<br />Accountability.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Know what is worth remembering—and which judgments need to change.</p>

      <div class="principles" aria-label="Editorial principles">
        <div><strong>01</strong><span>No publication quota.</span></div>
        <div><strong>02</strong><span>Evidence can change an existing judgment.</span></div>
        <div><strong>03</strong><span>Prior judgments remain visible when corrected.</span></div>
      </div>

      <nav class="editorial-toc" aria-label="Editorial policy sections">
        <a href="#scope">Scope</a>
        <a href="#roles">Roles</a>
        <a href="#gate">Signal gate</a>
        <a href="#revisions">Revisions</a>
        <a href="#corrections">Corrections</a>
        <a href="#predictions">Predictions</a>
        <a href="#reuse">Reuse</a>
        <a href="#submit">Submit evidence</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section id="scope"><h2>Scope, not a completeness claim</h2><p>GrepSignal's beta tracks material shifts across AI models, agents, tooling, and infrastructure, with a technical-builder bias. It is not comprehensive AI news. An absent event may be unreviewed, deferred, below the Signal threshold, or outside our scope. Zero new Signals is allowed; it is not itself proof of quality.</p></section>
    <section id="roles"><h2>Who does what</h2><p>ChatGPT performs semantic reading, evidence gathering, drafting and synthesis. Programs collect bounded inputs, preserve versions, prepare context and check structural and publication constraints; they do not establish truth. Editors accept publication and material judgment changes. Code/PR approval does not imply a human independently read every original source. Review records must state the actual work, actor and accepted version. Historical review scope that was not recorded remains unknown.</p><p>Local Explain is an optional reader-side aid, not an editor. Its output cannot change canonical intelligence.</p></section>
    <section id="gate"><h2>What passes the gate</h2><p>A Signal needs a bounded material change, claim-relevant evidence, a mechanism explaining why it matters, limitations and conditions that would change our view. We separate observed facts, source reports and our inferences. HN attention, repost counts, votes and search demand are not factual evidence.</p><p>A vendor source can establish a narrow statement about its own announcement or documented interface. It cannot independently establish general performance, broad adoption or causal impact. Source roles are claim- and event-specific. Multiple URLs do not automatically mean independent confirmation. Missing or unreadable evidence stays a visible gap. Anonymous claims and rumors may motivate research, but are not silently promoted into established facts.</p></section>
    <section id="revisions"><h2>Revisiting is not changing</h2><p>Threads are revisited when due or when material evidence appears, including counter-evidence. A completed review may leave the judgment unchanged. Inconclusive research and overdue work must remain visible. We do not require weakening, falsification or a daily publication quota. Historical recovery keeps the evidence date separate from the time we registered the judgment; it never rewrites a closed daily audit.</p></section>
    <section id="corrections"><h2>Corrections, replacements and withdrawals</h2><p>Report the exact claim and original evidence using the form below. An editor can request evidence, defer, explain non-adoption, or link an accepted revision/recovery. Material corrections keep the stable ID and prior version, state what changed and why, and identify affected linked judgments for re-review. A superseded record points to its replacement; a retracted record is visibly withdrawn. A falsified thesis is an evidence assessment, not a claim that every underlying historical fact never occurred.</p><p>Original text is normally retained with a clear notice and revision history. In exceptional privacy, security or rights cases, material may need removal; we retain a safe explanation rather than promise immutable exposure of harmful material. Cosmetic edits are distinguished from material corrections. There is no beta response-time SLA.</p></section>
    <section id="predictions"><h2>Predictions and public records</h2><p>A forecast needs a fixed claim, deadline, initial probability, success/failure criteria, resolution sources and an insufficient-evidence policy before public registration. Private drafts are not a public track record. At deadline an editor reviews evidence; insufficient evidence may remain unresolved. Programs calculate scores only after an eligible resolution, never decide outcomes. Original terms and prior resolutions remain visible. No example or drill is counted as a live prediction.</p></section>
    <section id="reuse"><h2>Reuse and attribution</h2><p>Our authorized original published intelligence is available under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">CC BY 4.0</a>; software remains Apache-2.0. Third-party source material is not relicensed. Credit GrepSignal, link the original record and license, and indicate changes. See <a href="https://github.com/cinic0101/grepsignal/blob/main/LICENSE-CONTENT.md">the content notice</a> for scope. Keeping IDs, limitations and correction links is recommended for responsible consumption, not an extra license restriction.</p></section>
    <section id="submit"><h2>Submit evidence or actual usage</h2><p>English, 繁體中文 and 简体中文 submissions are welcome. Original links and your explanation are sufficient; do not paste full articles, credentials, private documents or personal data. Issues are public, untrusted intake—not publication approval.</p><p class="actions"><a href={`${issues}?template=evidence.yml`}>Submit evidence / challenge →</a><a href={`${issues}?template=usage.yml`}>Report actual usage / integration →</a></p><p><a href={`${base}agents/`}>Machine-readable outputs →</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cinic0101/grepsignal/blob/main/docs/editorial-cases.md">Policy examples</a> · <a href="https://github.com/cinic0101/grepsignal/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md">Roadmap</a></p></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .editorial { max-width: 920px; padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 72px; }
  .editorial-head { padding-bottom: 8px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px); }
  .lead { font-size: 22px; max-width: 680px; }
  .principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-top: 34px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .principles div { display: grid; gap: 8px; padding: 18px 18px 18px 0; }
  .principles div + div { padding-left: 18px; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .principles strong { color: var(--accent); font: 800 10px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .principles span { font: 600 17px/1.35 Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
  .editorial-toc {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 800 10px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
  }
  .editorial-toc a { text-decoration: none; }
  .editorial-toc a:hover, .editorial-toc a:focus-visible { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  section { scroll-margin-top: 96px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 24px; margin-top: 36px; }
  h2 { font: 600 30px/1.2 Georgia, serif; }
  p { line-height: 1.75; }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .editorial { padding-top: 46px; }
    .principles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .principles div + div { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  }
</style>